      "subtitle": "",
      "duration_frames": 433,
      "transition": "none",
      "narration": "Scaling is not one technique but a stack: make services stateless, distribute with the right balancer at the right layer, detect failure with health checks and draining, close the loop with autoscaling, and defend against the herd and cascade under load. The engineers who build systems that survive traffic spikes aren't the ones with the biggest machines — they're the ones who assumed every node would fail and designed the fleet to route around it.",
